Source: pliwee
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Yuri Converso Sismotto <yuri.sismotto@gmail.com>
# The Rust floor is 1.88, measured from the committed lockfile rather than
# chosen: `time` 0.3.55 demands it and cargo's resolver refuses before
# compiling a line. desktop/Cargo.toml carries the derivation.
#
# The alternation is not decoration. MEASURED on each target's own archive:
#
#   Ubuntu 24.04 LTS   stock rustc 1.75      -> rustc-1.91 1.91.1  (alternative)
#   Ubuntu 26.04 LTS   stock rustc 1.93.1    -> satisfies (>= 1.88)
#   Debian 13 trixie   stock rustc 1.85.1    -> NEITHER. See README.source.
#
# So this line is satisfiable on both Ubuntu targets from their own archives,
# and **not** on stock trixie. That is stated here and in README.source rather
# than papered over with a lower floor that the code does not actually build
# against.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               rustc (>= 1.88) | rustc-1.91,
               cargo (>= 1.88) | cargo-1.91,
               pkg-config,
# The GUI is a workspace member and is always built. Each of these is here
# because something asks for it by name: the -sys crates resolve their C
# libraries through pkg-config, and desktop/gui/build.rs runs
# glib-compile-resources out of libglib2.0-dev.
               libgtk-4-dev (>= 4.12),
               libadwaita-1-dev (>= 1.5),
               libglib2.0-dev,
# override_dh_auto_test runs the full suite, and platform-linux's tray suites
# raise a real dbus-daemon rather than mocking the bus.
               dbus-daemon,
# install-desktop-metadata.sh validates the desktop entry and the AppStream
# metadata before installing them, and skips the check when the validator is
# absent. Declaring these makes that a build gate instead of a courtesy.
               desktop-file-utils,
               appstream-util
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/yurisismotto/pliwee
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/yurisismotto/pliwee
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/yurisismotto/pliwee.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: pliwee
Architecture: any
# No Rust at runtime. rustc and cargo are build dependencies only; the
# installed binaries need libc and, for the GUI, GTK — all resolved by
# ${shlibs:Depends} from the actual ELF headers.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
# Without UPower the daemon simply does not report this machine's own battery,
# which is the normal case on a desktop tower.
Recommends: upower
# Wayland clipboard. Suggests, and deliberately unversioned: `wl-copy
# --sensitive` is absent from wl-clipboard 2.2.1 on Debian and Ubuntu but
# present in Fedora's 2.2.1^git build — the same version string, different
# code. A versioned relation would be false on one distribution or the other
# whichever number was picked. The daemon reports honestly what its backend
# can do and works without it. Audit R5.
Suggests: wl-clipboard
# The OmniBridge -> Pliwee transition (ADR-0020). 1.1.0 is the first Pliwee
# version (rebrand plan, decision B4: adopted in Wave 7, to be confirmed by
# the owner before anything is published), written as a literal because it
# describes the one upgrade path from OmniBridge and must not move with later
# versions. The `~` admits a 1.1.0 pre-release as a Pliwee version too.
#
# Replaces: lets this package take over paths omnibridge 1.0.0 owned. Breaks:
# makes apt remove or upgrade that omnibridge rather than leave it half there.
# There is deliberately no Provides: omnibridge — the name is a real package
# again below, the transitional one, and a virtual package with the same name
# would give apt two answers to "install omnibridge".
Replaces: omnibridge (<< 1.1.0~)
Breaks: omnibridge (<< 1.1.0~)
Description: local-first device continuity between Android and Linux
 Pliwee connects an Android phone to this computer over the local network.
 It is local-first: there is no cloud service, no account and no telemetry.
 Devices authenticate each other with pinned public keys over TLS 1.3 after an
 explicit, human-confirmed pairing.
 .
 This package provides the user-session daemon and the pliwee command-line
 tool. The daemon runs unprivileged under systemd --user and never requires
 root. The desktop application ships separately, as pliwee-gui.
 .
 Pliwee was called OmniBridge until 1.0.0. An OmniBridge install upgrades to
 this package in place, keeping its device identity and every pairing.

Package: pliwee-gui
Architecture: any
# The exact build. The GUI speaks the daemon's control socket, so a version
# skew between the two is a protocol skew.
Depends: pliwee (= ${binary:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Replaces: omnibridge-gui (<< 1.1.0~)
Breaks: omnibridge-gui (<< 1.1.0~)
Description: desktop application for Pliwee
 The Pliwee desktop application: pairing, the device list, transfers, the
 Quick Panel and per-capability grants.
 .
 It is not a resident process. It is started when a window is wanted - from the
 application menu, from the tray item the daemon publishes, or by the session
 bus through D-Bus activation - and it exits when the window is closed. The
 daemon remains the only long-lived Pliwee process.

# --- transitional packages ---------------------------------------------------
#
# MEASURED (rebrand Wave 7 report, D1/D2, apt on Ubuntu 24.04): with Replaces:,
# Breaks: and Provides: alone, `apt upgrade` on an OmniBridge 1.0.0 install
# upgraded nothing — apt does not install a package that nothing depends on.
# With these two, `apt upgrade` upgrades omnibridge and omnibridge-gui to
# 1.1.0 and installs pliwee and pliwee-gui as their dependencies, and the old
# packages' postrm runs with `upgrade`, not `remove`. `apt-get upgrade` keeps
# them back (they add a dependency); `apt-get dist-upgrade` takes them.
#
# Both are empty and removable once Pliwee is installed. The ${binary:Version}
# pin keeps each one moving in step with the package it points at.

Package: omnibridge
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
Depends: pliwee (>= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: transitional package - OmniBridge is now Pliwee
 OmniBridge was renamed Pliwee. This empty package upgrades an OmniBridge
 install to Pliwee, and can be removed once pliwee is installed.

Package: omnibridge-gui
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
Depends: pliwee-gui (>= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: transitional package - OmniBridge is now Pliwee (desktop application)
 OmniBridge was renamed Pliwee. This empty package upgrades an OmniBridge
 desktop application install to pliwee-gui, and can be removed once
 pliwee-gui is installed.
